  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner-decision 2026-08-27">Implement **option (C)**. Do NOT implement (A) or (B), and do NOT re-open the decision — it was made against the accurate framing after the escalation note's scope objection was found stale. If execution surfaces a fact that genuinely invalidates (C), that is an escalation (see `escalation`), not a quiet pivot.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The authorization key and the container MUST be the same value. The route takes `(entity, recordId)`; the server resolves the container from that record via 075's resolver. A route that accepts BOTH a record and a container is a failed implementation of this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§11 reuse">Do not build a new record-authorization mechanism. `Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs` already authorizes `(entityType, recordId)` for the caller via `CallerRecordAccessProbe` — extend that, or state in ≤2 sentences why it cannot serve. A second probe is a review failure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">A secure record with no container FAILS CLOSED and loudly — never a fallback to the BU or archive container. This is 075's behaviour; your job is not to soften it at the route.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Authorization is an endpoint filter, not handler code and not middleware.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Delete rather than convert where the path is dead — the chunked OBO pair (§1). Verify the `GET /api/obo/containers/{id}/drive` 404 yourself before deleting.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The creation wizard must not write `sprk_containerid` at all (W1), and the DocumentUploadWizard write-back (W2) must go. Removing the write is required, not conditioning it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No client code contains an `issecure` test, and no client code names a container for an upload. Either one in the final diff is a review failure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-074">Delete the three `Pending` OBO upload waivers (`RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:235/240/244`). Do NOT convert any of them to `Permanent` to make a build go green — that inverts the forcing function.</constraint>
    <constraint source="deploy">State the client+BFF ship-together obligation in the PR description AND the task notes. This is the outage risk.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">State the Placement Justification citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; verify publish size (≤60 MB ceiling; baseline ~44.96 MB incl. PDBs — state the PDB convention) and run the CVE check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §12">PCF builds use `npm run build:prod`, never `npm run build`. Bump PCF versions in all four locations if any PCF ships.</constraint>
  </constraints>

